without_squoze.fullPatch:
Root cause: routing resolved the path by reading `r.URL.RawPath` and falling back to `r.URL.Path`. `net/url` only populates `RawPath` when the default encoding of `Path` doesn't round-trip, so for many encoded paths it is empty and matching happens against the *decoded* path — turning `%2F` into a real separator and splitting one segment into two. It is also left stale when middleware rewrites `r.URL.Path`. `EscapedPath()` handles both: it returns `RawPath` only when it is a valid encoding of `Path`, and otherwise re-escapes `Path`.

